# Manual requests for Payments.Api. Run them one by one from top to bottom in VS Code (REST Client extension),
# Visual Studio or Rider.
# docker compose: http://localhost:8080; dotnet run: http://localhost:5113.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@merchant = shop-1

### Health: the API is up and MongoDB answers ping
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 1. Create a payment -> 201 Created, ETag: "0"
# Change the key to create another payment.
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: order-1001

{
  "merchantId": "{{merchant}}",
  "customerId": "c-42",
  "amount": 25.00,
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 2. The same request again (a client retry) -> 200 OK with the SAME payment, no second document
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: order-1001

{
  "merchantId": "{{merchant}}",
  "customerId": "c-42",
  "amount": 25.00,
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 3. The same key with a different amount -> 422 Unprocessable Entity
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: order-1001

{
  "merchantId": "{{merchant}}",
  "customerId": "c-42",
  "amount": 99.00,
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 4. No Idempotency-Key -> 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "merchantId": "{{merchant}}",
  "customerId": "c-42",
  "amount": 25.00,
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 5. Read the payment -> 200 OK, ETag: "0"
GET {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{create.response.body.$.id}}

### 6. Capture with the version we read -> 200 OK, status Captured, ETag: "1"
# Also publishes PaymentCaptured through the outbox: docker compose logs api shows "PaymentCaptured received".
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/capture
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "0"

{
  "provider": "Adyen"
}

### 7. Capture again with the old version -> 412 Precondition Failed (someone changed the payment)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/capture
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "0"

{
  "provider": "Adyen"
}

### 8. Capture with the current version -> 409 Conflict (already Captured)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/capture
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "1"

{
  "provider": "Adyen"
}

### 9. Capture without If-Match -> 428 Precondition Required
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/capture
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "provider": "Adyen"
}

### 10. Merchant history, newest first (LINQ, index merchantId + createdAt)
GET {{baseUrl}}/merchants/{{merchant}}/payments?limit=10

### 11. Merchant history in a date range (dates without an offset are UTC)
GET {{baseUrl}}/merchants/{{merchant}}/payments?from=2026-01-01&to=2027-01-01&limit=10

### 12. Captured totals per currency (aggregation pipeline)
GET {{baseUrl}}/merchants/{{merchant}}/totals

#######################################################################################################################
# The same endpoints with the EF Core provider: prefix /ef. Same collection, same HTTP rules; differences:
#   capture - read + SaveChanges with a concurrency token; the event is published after SaveChanges, without outbox;
#   totals  - GroupBy is not supported: all captured payments are loaded and grouped in memory (see the api log).
#######################################################################################################################

### EF 1. Create a payment through EF Core -> 201 Created, Location: /ef/payments/{id}
# @name efCreate
POST {{baseUrl}}/ef/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ef-order-1001

{
  "merchantId": "{{merchant}}",
  "customerId": "c-42",
  "amount": 10.00,
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### EF 2. Read it through the DRIVER endpoint -> 200: both implementations share the documents
GET {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{efCreate.response.body.$.id}}

### EF 3. Capture through EF Core -> 200 OK, ETag: "1"
POST {{baseUrl}}/ef/payments/{{efCreate.response.body.$.id}}/capture
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "0"

{
  "provider": "Klarna"
}

### EF 4. Capture again with the old version -> 412 (concurrency token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ef/payments/{{efCreate.response.body.$.id}}/capture
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "0"

{
  "provider": "Klarna"
}

### EF 5. Merchant history through EF Core (LINQ, same result as request 10)
GET {{baseUrl}}/ef/merchants/{{merchant}}/payments?limit=10

### EF 6. Totals through EF Core (same result as request 12, computed in memory)
GET {{baseUrl}}/ef/merchants/{{merchant}}/totals
